<title>NEW ZEALAND: DB Group reports NZ$17.16 mln H1 profit.</title>
<headline>DB Group reports NZ$17.16 mln H1 profit.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr result to March 31.</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   17.16 vs 16.0</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)				 4.25 vs 5.24</p>
<p>    Div (cents)				  8.0 vs 2.0</p>
<p>    Turnover				  351.01 vs 351.35</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			    29.54 vs 27.26</p>
<p>    Tax					  10.07 vs 9.16</p>
<p>    Equity earnings		    loss 0.95 vs 0.86 loss</p>
<p>Dividend carries full imputation credit.</p>
<p>Pay date July 11</p>
<p>Reg date June 27</p>
<p>    Ex div   June 30</p>
<p>Note - DB Group Ltd is a brewing company majority owned through a Heineken Nv, Fraser and Neave Ltd joint venture. Market expectations were for a net profit between NZ$15-16 million. DB Group restructured its balance sheet in May, resulting in the cancellation of three out of four fully-paid shares.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
